Refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for the description of the
"nvinferserver" plugin.

Dependencies:
- Triton Inference Server library (/opt/tritonserver/lib/libtritonserver.so)
- Matching Triton26.10 gRPC client SDK for x86 and genericSBSA/Spark
- Separately qualified JetPack7.2.2/TRT11.4.1 client/server inputs for Jetson
- Google Protobuf compiler matching the selected Triton client SDK's headers
  and protobuf libraries (do not assume the older v3.21.12 compiler matches)
- Half - Half precision floating point C++ library v2.1.0 

Please ensure that the above dependencies are installed and update corresponding
paths in the Makefile if required.
Current set paths are as follows:
PROTOBUF_BIN_DIR ?= /opt/proto/bin
TRITON_GRPC_CLIENT ?= /opt/tritonclient
HALF_PRECISION_LIB ?= /opt/half

When the selected client SDK supplies include/model_config.pb.h, the build uses
that header instead of regenerating the older bundled Triton schema. Older SDKs
without that header retain local schema generation. PROTOBUF_BIN_DIR must select
the matching protoc for the SDK in either case; DeepStream's own protobuf files
are regenerated with it. Rebuild both this library and gst-nvinferserver when
changing providers; headers, generated code and client/server binaries must agree.

For protobuf 6 and newer, the core uses the matching SDK's static client, gRPC,
protobuf, Abseil and upb archives as one private runtime. Supply the complete SDK,
not just libgrpcclient.so. Its generated model types cannot safely be reflected
using a second private protobuf runtime. The build keeps archive/header symbols
private while exporting DeepStream's own generated types and typed helpers.
Older providers retain their existing shared-client link. Rebuild dependent
protobuf consumers as well; do not reuse objects linked to a previous provider.

For installing the Triton gRPC client library and the protobuf compiler please
check the steps in /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/sources/gst-plugins/gst-nvinferserver/README 

Installing Half v2.1.0:
mkdir /opt/half
wget https://sourceforge.net/projects/half/files/half/2.1.0/half-2.1.0.zip
unzip half-2.1.0.zip -d /opt/half/
rm half-2.1.0.zip

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing the plugin:
Export or set in Makefile the appropriate CUDA_VER

Run make and sudo make install

NOTE: To compile the sources, run make with "sudo" or root permission.
